---
/* The command palette: Ctrl+K, Cmd+K or / opens it, and so does the "Search" button in the
   closing's site index and in the top line's card (PaletteOpen.astro), so nobody needs the
   keyboard to find it. Type to filter pages, case studies, sector pages, prices, journal posts
   and a few actions; arrows, Enter and Escape work, and every row is a real link or button, so a
   mouse or a finger works too.

   It is a native <dialog>, so focus is trapped and handed back by the browser. The rows are built
   by src/scripts/palette.js from /peek.json (the same file the link previews read), fetched the
   first time it opens. It is a card from the kit: lettered K in two corners, hairline rows. The
   look and the spring are in src/styles/elevate-b.css.

   Without script nothing can open it, so its buttons are hidden then; every page it lists is in
   the dock and the closing anyway. */
---

<dialog class="pal card keyed" data-pal aria-label="Search the site">
  <span class="pip" aria-hidden="true">
    K
  </span>
  <span class="pip flip" aria-hidden="true">
    K
  </span>
  <div class="pal-top">
    <label class="label" for="pal-q">
      Search the site
    </label>
    <div class="pal-field">
      <input
        id="pal-q"
        class="pal-q"
        type="text"
        role="combobox"
        aria-expanded="true"
        aria-controls="pal-list"
        aria-autocomplete="list"
        autocomplete="off"
        autocapitalize="off"
        spellcheck="false"
        enterkeyhint="go"
        placeholder="A page, a client, a price"
        data-pal-q
      />
      <button class="pal-x" type="button" data-pal-close>
        Close
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="pal-list" id="pal-list" role="listbox" aria-label="Results" data-pal-list></div>
  <p class="pal-none" data-pal-none hidden>
    Nothing by that name. Try a client, a page or the word prices.
  </p>
  <p class="pal-say" aria-live="polite" data-pal-say></p>
  <div class="pal-foot">
    <span class="pal-keys label" aria-hidden="true">
      <span>
        <kbd>&uarr;</kbd>
        <kbd>&darr;</kbd> Move
      </span>
      <span>
        <kbd>Enter</kbd> Open
      </span>
      <span>
        <kbd>Esc</kbd> Close
      </span>
    </span>
    {/* A one-key shortcut has to be something a visitor can switch off (WCAG 2.1.4). */}
    <button class="pal-slash label" type="button" aria-pressed="true" data-pal-slash>
      <kbd>/</kbd> opens this
    </button>
  </div>
</dialog>
